---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Centralizing Supplier Communication Across Channels - Marker"
>
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a
        href="/case-studies"
        class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground"
      >
        <svg
          class="mr-1 h-4 w-4"
          fill="none"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
        >
          <path
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span
        class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary"
      >
        DTC Footwear
      </span>
      <h1
        class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl"
      >
        Centralizing Supplier Communication Across Channels
      </h1>

      <div
        class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm"
      >
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Direct-to-consumer footwear brand sourcing from Europe and
              Asia</span
            >
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Supply chain analyst managing vendor relationships across
              multiple regions</span
            >
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span
            >
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Communication scattered across email, WhatsApp, and WeChat with
              no central record of supplier interactions</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          This DTC footwear brand works with factories in both Europe and Asia,
          each with different communication norms. European suppliers preferred
          email. Asian factories used WeChat. Internal discussions happened on
          Slack. As the supply chain analyst described it: there was "never a
          true understanding of where the information is."
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The consequences were tangible. When a critical material — suede, in
          one case — was delayed, the update on revised ship timelines was buried
          across channels. Getting a clear picture of where things stood required
          manually checking multiple apps and chasing down colleagues who might
          have received updates on a different platform.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The supply chain analyst estimated that most of his time was consumed
          by administrative work: reconciling invoices, checking factory payment
          status, processing returns, and verifying that factory invoices matched
          PO terms. The work he wanted to focus on — cost optimization,
          customer experience, new vendor evaluation — was perpetually deferred.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Marker connects to email, WhatsApp, and WeChat, bringing all supplier
          communication into a single timeline regardless of channel. Each
          message is linked to the relevant product, purchase order, or
          supplier — creating the central record that the team lacked.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          When a factory sends a ship date update via WeChat, it appears
          alongside the email thread about the same PO and the WhatsApp message
          about the material sourcing. The team no longer needs to reconstruct
          context from multiple apps. For invoice reconciliation, Marker can
          surface the relevant PO terms and flag discrepancies, reducing the
          manual checking that consumed the analyst's days.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          For a brand with a 5-7 month concept-to-shelf timeline and 90-130 day
          production lead times, even small improvements in communication
          clarity can prevent costly delays. When the team can see all
          interactions with a supplier in one place — including payment history,
          quality check notes, and outstanding issues — they can make faster,
          better-informed decisions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Unified timeline across email, WhatsApp, and WeChat — no more
              switching between apps to find supplier updates</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Every message automatically linked to the relevant product, PO,
              or supplier for instant context</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Invoice and PO term discrepancies surfaced automatically,
              reducing manual reconciliation work</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Ship date changes and material delays visible in one place,
              enabling faster response to disruptions</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Analyst time freed from administrative tasks, allowing focus on
              cost optimization and vendor strategy</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section
        class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">
          See how Marker brings all your supplier communication into one place.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/book-demo"
          class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2"
        >
          Book a Demo
        </a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
